# {{ itsm_kb_vm_provisioning_title }}

## Step 1 — Open ITSM service request

Open catalog **{{ itsm_apache_stack_request_template_name }}** in itsm-app. Ask the user for `vm_name`, `cpus`, `mem`, `app_repo`; optional `app_branch`, `rpm_packages`, `app_clone_path`, `enabled_services`, `exposed_port`. On submit, itsm-app returns `itsm_service_request_ref` (REQ-*) and `itsm_change_ref` (CHG-*). **User does not provide these refs** — take them from ITSM after submit.

## Step 2 — Launch AAP workflow

Launch **{{ aap_apache_stack_pipeline_workflow }}** (org **{{ aap_apache_stack_pipeline_organization }}**). Use step-1 refs plus user stack fields. Never ask the user for refs or invent them.

| Extra var | Req | Source |
|-----------|-----|--------|
| `itsm_change_ref` | yes | Step 1 (not user) |
| `itsm_service_request_ref` | no | Step 1 (not user) |
| `vm_name` | yes | User |
| `cpus` | yes | User |
| `mem` | yes | User |
| `app_repo` | yes | User |
| `app_branch` | no | User, optional |
| `apache_app_rpm_packages` | no | ITSM **RPM packages** field (or playbook default `httpd,git`) |
| `apache_app_docroot` | no | ITSM **Repository clone path** field (or playbook default `/var/www/html`) |
| `apache_app_enabled_services` | no | ITSM **Service to enable** field (or playbook default `httpd`) |
| `apache_exposure_service_port` | no | ITSM **Port to expose** field (or playbook default `80`) |

Map ITSM service-request specification keys to AAP extra vars when launching from catalog data:

| ITSM request field | AAP extra var |
|--------------------|---------------|
| RPM packages (`rpm_packages`) | `apache_app_rpm_packages` |
| Repository clone path (`app_clone_path`) | `apache_app_docroot` |
| Service to enable (`enabled_services`) | `apache_app_enabled_services` |
| Port to expose (`exposed_port`) | `apache_exposure_service_port` |

When a **Generic Application** ITSM asset exists for the VM and repository, the bot also passes the same extra vars from the asset (overriding playbook defaults when set):

| ITSM asset field | AAP extra var |
|------------------|---------------|
| RPM packages | `apache_app_rpm_packages` |
| Service to enable | `apache_app_enabled_services` |
| Repository clone path | `apache_app_docroot` |
| Port to expose | `apache_exposure_service_port` |

`apache_app_rpm_packages` replaces `apache_app_package` / `apache_app_git_package`; `apache_app_enabled_services` replaces `apache_app_service`.

Example:
```
itsm_change_ref: CHG-6
itsm_service_request_ref: REQ-3
vm_name: server01
cpus: 2
mem: 4
app_repo: AIOps_App
app_branch: main
apache_app_rpm_packages: httpd,git
apache_app_docroot: /var/www/html
apache_app_enabled_services: httpd
apache_exposure_service_port: 80
```

